## Why This Is Asked
Autocompletion is common in editors and apps; this tests a lightweight data structure for fast prefix queries and shows practical space/time trade-offs.

## Key Concepts
- Trie structure with per-node prefix counts
- O(len(prefix)) lookup
- Space proportional to total characters in dictionary
- Edge cases: empty prefix, missing path

## Code Example
```javascript
class TrieNode {
  constructor() {
    this.children = new Map();
    this.count = 0;
  }
}
class Trie {
  constructor() {
    this.root = new TrieNode();
  }
  insert(word) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const ch of word) {
      if (!node.children.has(ch)) node.children.set(ch, new TrieNode());
      node = node.children.get(ch);
      node.count++;
    }
  }
  countWithPrefix(prefix) {
    let node = this.root;
    for (const ch of prefix) {
      if (!node.children.has(ch)) return 0;
      node = node.children.get(ch);
    }
    return node.count;
  }
}
```

